═══════════ railway postgres --help ═══════════
Manage Postgres features: point-in-time recovery, high availability, and connection pooling

Usage: railway postgres [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  pitr       Manage point-in-time recovery (continuous backups)
  ha         Manage high-availability clustering
  pgbouncer  Manage PgBouncer connection pooling
  history    Show the local audit trail of Postgres operations
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -s, --service <SERVICE>          Service name or ID (defaults to linked service)
  -e, --environment <ENVIRONMENT>  Environment to use (defaults to linked environment)
  -p, --project <PROJECT_ID>       Project ID to use (defaults to linked project)
      --json                       Output in JSON format
  -h, --help                       Print help
  -V, --version                    Print version

Examples:

  railway postgres pitr status --service postgres
  railway postgres pitr enable --service postgres
  railway postgres ha status --service postgres
  railway postgres ha convert --service postgres --replicas 2
  railway postgres pgbouncer add --service postgres --pool-mode transaction

Automation notes:
  --service/--environment/--project/--json apply to every subcommand below `railway postgres`.
  Actions that change config (enable/disable/convert/revert/add/remove/configure/scale) commit and deploy by default; pass --no-deploy to commit the config change without triggering deploys (it then applies on each affected service's next deploy).


═══════════ railway api --help ═══════════
Query the Railway public GraphQL API.

Use `railway api search <term>` and `railway api describe <name>` to inspect the schema before running a query.

Usage: railway api [OPTIONS] [QUERY] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  schema    Print the live GraphQL introspection schema
  search    Search GraphQL types and fields
  describe  Describe a GraphQL type or field
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [QUERY]
          GraphQL query or mutation document. If omitted, stdin is used when piped

Options:
  -f, --file <PATH>
          Read the GraphQL document from a file. Use '-' to read from stdin

      --variables <JSON|@PATH>
          JSON variables object, or @PATH to read JSON from a file. Use @- for stdin

      --var <KEY=VALUE>
          Set a typed variable as KEY=VALUE. VALUE is parsed as JSON when possible

      --raw-var <KEY=VALUE>
          Set a string variable as KEY=VALUE

      --operation-name <NAME>
          GraphQL operation name to execute when the document contains multiple operations

      --compact
          Print compact JSON

      --allow-errors
          Exit successfully even when the GraphQL response has an errors array

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version


═══════════ railway service source --help ═══════════
Connect or disconnect a service source

Usage: railway service source <COMMAND>

Commands:
  connect     Connect a service to a GitHub repo or Docker image
  disconnect  Disconnect the service from its current source
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Examples:

  railway service source connect --repo owner/repo --branch main --service web
  railway service source connect --repo owner/repo --service web --json
  railway service source connect --image nginx:latest --service web
  railway service source disconnect --service web

Automation notes:
  Use --branch for repos that are not visible through the Railway GitHub App.
  GitHub sources are connected at the service level and create deployment triggers for matching project environments.


